---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StoreBadge from '../components/StoreBadge.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Love Desire"
  description="Why we built a couples app for two, not a social platform for many."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-16">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-muted font-bold mb-3 text-center">About</p>
    <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-tight text-burgundy text-center">
      For two,<br />
      <em class="font-normal">not for many</em>.
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-16 flex flex-col gap-8 text-burgundy/85 leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <p>
        Most apps that touch relationships end up looking like everything else. Feeds, matches, streaks, points, notifications for the sake of notifications. That works for platforms with millions of strangers. It doesn't work for you and one other person.
      </p>

      <p>
        Love Desire is for two people who are already together. There's nothing to swipe, nothing to browse, no one else here. You share a 6-digit invite code with your person once, and then it's just the two of you inside.
      </p>

      <p>
        The features cover what actually keeps people close. <span class="italic">Rhythms</span> like mood check-ins, Sunday Check-in, and Moments. <span class="italic">Play</span> like Truth or Dare, Would You Rather, Fantasy Wishes, and Activity Cards. <span class="italic">Quiet insight</span> like The Lovers intimacy quiz, Sensate Focus, and Relationship Pulse. Some of it is silly, some of it is deep. Use what fits the week you're in.
      </p>

      <p>
        Your data is visible to the two of you and no one else. We don't sell it, share it, or feed it to a model. Explicit content sits behind an 18+ attestation and the paid tier. One subscription covers both partners, because subscription belongs to the couple, not the individual.
      </p>

      <p>
        Built and maintained by one person. Feedback goes straight to my inbox.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-border">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-24 text-center flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl text-burgundy max-w-xl leading-tight">
        Try it together.
      </h2>
      <div class="pt-2">
        <StoreBadge />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
